				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\bar{d}$$\end{document}d¯, axonal delay. b, Dual memory pathway abstraction. At the algorithmic level, each layer maintains a shared, low-dimensional state that captures slow contextual dynamics and modulates fast spiking activity. At the hardware level, this separation is mirrored by a heterogeneous accelerator that keeps the compact state on-chip and fuses sparse and dense computations for efficient execution.
Source data

We benchmarked four spiking network architectures: FSNN, RSNN, DSNN and our DMP-SNN (Table 1). Feedforward SNNs fail on long-range structure tasks (11.3% on PS-MNIST). Recurrence in RSNNs improves temporal integration (71.0% on PS-MNIST; 71.4% on SHD) but scales as \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
